---
import MainLayout from '../layouts/MainLayout.astro';
import '../styles/r3.css';
import { links } from '../data/links';
import { careerProgression, impactCases, specialties } from '../data/portfolio';
const resumeHref = '/resume/Corrine-J-Blackthorn-Resume.pdf';
---
<MainLayout
  title="Experience | Corrine J Blackthorn"
  description="Review Corrine J. Blackthorn's professional background, cybersecurity achievements, identity governance expertise, and resume."
>
  <section class="content-section">
    <div class="container split">
      <div>
        <span class="kicker">Professional experience</span>
        <h1>Identity governance, security, and systems thinking.</h1>
        <p>My career spans more than two decades in information technology, including identity and access engineering, governance, security, technical operations, and audit support. My approach combines architectural thinking with an understanding of how controls work in day-to-day operations.</p>
        <p>The examples here demonstrate the kinds of problems I solve. The downloadable resume provides the more formal employment history.</p>
        <div class="section-actions">
          <a class="button dark" href={resumeHref} download>Download resume</a>
          <a class="button" href={links.personal.linkedin} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">LinkedIn</a>
          <a class="button" href={links.personal.github} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">GitHub</a>
        </div>
      </div>
      <article class="card compact-card">
        <span class="kicker">Areas of impact</span>
        <h2>Access, accountability, and clarity.</h2>
        <p>My most meaningful work is often at the intersection of identity lifecycle, security controls, governance processes, and organizational change.</p>
        <p>I am especially interested in roles or collaborations where technical architecture and the quality of decisions matter equally.</p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="content-section section-soft">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section-heading"><span class="kicker">Career progression</span><h2>From operating systems to governing access.</h2><p>A thematic progression through the work. Refer to the resume for dates, employers, and full role history.</p></div>
      <ol class="career-timeline">
        {careerProgression.map(item => <li><span class="feature-category">{item.stage}</span><h3>{item.title}</h3><p>{item.description}</p></li>)}
      </ol>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="content-section">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section-heading"><span class="kicker">Selected achievements</span><h2>Work backed by outcomes.</h2><p>These examples are limited to general and previously public descriptions. They are not disclosures of client or employer systems.</p></div>
      <div class="grid">
        {impactCases.map(item => <article class="card compact-card"><h3>{item.title}</h3><p>{item.result}</p><a class="feature-link" href="/technology/">Explore the approach</a></article>)}
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="content-section section-soft">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section-heading"><span class="kicker">Expertise</span><h2>The disciplines I connect.</h2><p>Clear controls depend on both deep technical knowledge and an understanding of organizational goals.</p></div>
      <div class="grid">{specialties.map(area => <article class="card compact-card"><h3>{area.title}</h3><p>{area.description}</p></article>)}</div>
      <div class="section-actions"><a class="button dark" href={resumeHref} download>Download full resume</a><a class="button" href={links.personal.linkedin} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Connect on LinkedIn</a></div>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="quote-band"><div class="container"><blockquote>The architecture matters. So do the people, the evidence, and the decisions that keep it working.</blockquote></div></section>
</MainLayout>
